[Event "Evans Gambit"]
[StudyName "Evans Gambit"]
[ChapterName "Evans Gambit Accepted"]
[Orientation "white"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 {The Evans Gambit: give a pawn to win time and build a huge centre. It was a favourite of 19th-century attackers and still scores well today.} Bxb4 5. c3 {Hits the bishop and threatens d4.} Ba5 {The most common retreat.} 6. d4 exd4 7. O-O {Sacrifice a second pawn for a lead in development.} d6 8. cxd4 Bb6 9. Nc3 Na5 10. Bg5 f6 11. Bf4 {White has a big centre and open lines against the king.}

[Event "Evans Gambit"]
[StudyName "Evans Gambit"]
[ChapterName "Accepted: the other retreat 5...Bc5"]
[Orientation "white"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 Bxb4 5. c3 Bc5 6. d4 exd4 7. O-O Nf6 8. Nxd4 Nxd4 9. cxd4 Bb6 10. Nc3 {Active pieces and a strong centre: ideas like e5 and Bg5 follow.}

[Event "Evans Gambit"]
[StudyName "Evans Gambit"]
[ChapterName "Evans Gambit Declined: 4...Bb6"]
[Orientation "white"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 Bb6 {Black declines and keeps the pawn.} 5. a4 a6 6. Nc3 Nf6 7. d3 d6 8. Bg5 h6 9. Bh4 {A comfortable game for White.}
